==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|sagacité|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|sagacitas|lang=la||sagaciousness}}, from {{term|sagax|lang=la||of quick perception, acute, sagacious}}, from {{term|sagire|lang=la||to perceive by the senses}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/səˈɡæsəti/|/səˈgæsɪti/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|sagacities}}

# The quality of being [[sage]], [[wise]], or able to make good decisions.

====Synonyms====
* [[wisdom]]
* [[sagaciousness]]

====Related terms====
* [[sagacious]]

